## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where Google Meet realtime audio bridges could accept malformed base64 audio chunks from direct `googlemeet.chrome` calls or paired-node `pullAudio` responses.

## Why This Change Was Made

The Google Meet audio bridge now uses one owner-local base64 validation helper before policy forwarding, node-host playback, and realtime provider input. Valid audio chunks still flow through unchanged.

## User Impact

Malformed bridge audio is rejected or treated as a transient input failure instead of being decoded into arbitrary bytes and sent to playback or the realtime provider.

## Evidence

- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/google-meet/src/node-invoke-policy.test.ts extensions/google-meet/node-host.test.ts extensions/google-meet/index.test.ts`: 159 tests passed.
- `node --import tsx --input-type=module -`: imported the real policy and realtime bridge modules, proving invalid direct `pushAudio` does not dispatch and invalid pulled audio does not reach `provider.sendAudio` while a valid control chunk still does.

```text
$ node --import tsx --input-type=module -
{
  "productionPath": [
    "createGoogleMeetChromeNodeInvokePolicy",
    "startNodeRealtimeAudioBridge",
    "runtime.nodes.invoke(pullAudio)",
    "provider.sendAudio"
  ],
  "policy": {
    "invalidOk": false,
    "invalidMessage": "base64 must be a valid audio payload",
    "invalidDispatches": 0,
    "validOk": true,
    "validDispatches": 1
  },
  "realtime": {
    "pullCount": 3,
    "providerAudioChunks": [
      [
        5,
        4,
        3
      ]
    ],
    "malformedChunkForwarded": false,
    "validChunkForwarded": true,
    "lastInputBytes": 3,
    "consecutiveInputErrors": 0
  }
}
```

